From: Platina Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: restore SDM660 ISPIF and CSI mux

The SDM660 resource table provides ISPIF and camss-ispif.c already handles
CAMSS_660, but camss_probe() omits this version from allocation. The null
ISPIF silently creates a direct CSID -> VFE graph which does not match the
hardware. Include SDM660 in the existing ISPIF allocation condition.
Observed on Platina: sensor identity succeeds, direct graph never delivers
SOF and times out. This change restores the hardware path, not a bypass. Map the existing
SDM660 CSIPHY clock-mux resource as on the other legacy ISPIF platforms.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -5388,7 +5388,8 @@
 	if (camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x16 ||
 	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x39 ||
 	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x53 ||
-	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x96) {
+	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x96 ||
+	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_660) {
 		camss->ispif = devm_kcalloc(dev, 1, sizeof(*camss->ispif), GFP_KERNEL);
 		if (!camss->ispif)
 			return -ENOMEM;
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
@@ -606,7 +606,8 @@
 	if (camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x16 ||
 	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x39 ||
 	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x53 ||
-	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x96) {
+	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_8x96 ||
+	    camss->res->version == CAMSS_660) {
 		csiphy->base_clk_mux =
 			devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname(pdev, res->reg[1]);
 		if (IS_ERR(csiphy->base_clk_mux))
